@startuml find-usages-sequence
title Find Usages — query flow

actor User
participant "IdeApp\n(app.rs)" as UI
participant "LspBridge" as Bridge
participant "LspClient\nevent loop" as Client
participant "rust-analyzer" as Server

User -> UI: click "Find Usages"\n(or Alt+F7 / Option+F7,\nor Cmd+Click a symbol)
UI -> UI: find_usages()\n(byte_offset_to_position)
UI -> Bridge: find_references(path, position)
Bridge -> Bridge: references.clear()\nfinding_references = true
Bridge -> Client: send(LspRequest::References)

alt not yet initialized
  Client -> Client: queue in pending[]
else ready
  Client -> Client: allocate id N\npending_references_id = N
  Client -> Server: textDocument/references\n(id=N, includeDeclaration=true)
end

== later: a second query supersedes the first ==
User -> UI: click "Find Usages" again (different symbol)
UI -> Bridge: find_references(path2, position2)
Bridge -> Client: send(LspRequest::References)
Client -> Client: allocate id N+1\npending_references_id = N+1
Client -> Server: textDocument/references (id=N+1)

Server --> Client: response id=N (stale)
Client -> Client: id != pending_references_id\n=> dropped, no event

Server --> Client: response id=N+1
Client -> Client: parse result (permissive:\nnull/empty/unparseable => [])
Client -> Client: validate each Location's path\nagainst project_root; skip failures
Client -> Bridge: LspEvent::References { locations }
Bridge -> Bridge: references = locations\nfinding_references = false
UI -> UI: Usages panel re-renders

User -> UI: click a usage row
UI -> UI: open_usage(path, position)\n(open_file + pending_cursor_offset)

@enduml
